§§ `Paragraph 11: powers of arrest under the Asylum and Immigration (Treatment of Claimants, etc.) Act 2004`

-- src:367 | Powers of arrest under Asylum and Immigration (Treatment of Claimants, etc.) Act 2004 (c. 19)
-- src:368 | 11 (1) Nothing in paragraph 35 of Schedule 1 affects the power of arrest conferred by section 14 of the Asylum and Immigration (Treatment of Claimants, etc.) Act 2004 in relation to an offence partly committed before the commencement of that paragraph.
-- src:369 | (2) An offence is partly committed before the commencement of paragraph 35 of Schedule 1 if—
-- src:370 | (a) a relevant event occurs before its commencement, and
-- src:371 | (b) another relevant event occurs on or after its commencement.
-- src:372 | (3) “Relevant event”, in relation to an offence, means any act, omission or other event (including any result of one or more acts or omissions) proof of which is required for conviction of the offence.
@ref Fraud Act 2006 Schedule 2 paragraph 11(1) (src:368)
GIVEN events IS A LIST OF DATE
      `the day paragraph 35 of Schedule 1 came into force` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Schedule 2 paragraph 11(1): paragraph 35 of Schedule 1 does not affect the power of arrest conferred by section 14 of the 2004 Act` events `the day paragraph 35 of Schedule 1 came into force` MEANS
    -- This is a power of an immigration officer, not of the person; it is encoded only so that the
    -- saving is not lost.  Paragraph 11(2) and (3) are stated once with paragraph 3(2) and (3).
    `Schedule 2 paragraphs 3(2) and 11(2): the offence was partly committed before the commencement` events `the day paragraph 35 of Schedule 1 came into force`

§§ `Paragraph 2: inert`

-- Paragraph 2 says that section 10 (increase in penalty for fraudulent trading) does not affect
-- the penalty for an offence committed before section 10 comes into force.  Section 10 is blank in
-- this text and the penalty it concerned is the Companies Act's, which is not among the sources,
-- so paragraph 2 decides nothing here.  The quotation is kept for the reader.
-- src:345 | Increase in penalty for fraudulent trading
-- src:346 | 2 Section 10 does not affect the penalty for any offence committed before that section comes into force.
